Sweep the rear camera's link at runtime, without recompiling

The rear camera's 435,2 MHz link_freq is DEDUCED from the PLLs in the vendor
file (19,2/3 x 272 / 2 / 2 = 435,2 MHz DDR), not measured. If the sensor emits
at a rate different from the one declared to the CSIPHY there can be no sync and
the CSID sees nothing, which is exactly what happens:

    the sensor emits           0x0100 = 0x01, twelve registers out of twelve
                               matching the vendor
    the CSID receives nothing  packets=0, crc=0, bytes_rdi0=0

And these are already ruled out, with validated instruments:

    the clocks                 csiphy0_clk 400 MHz, cphy_rx 400,
                               csi0phytimer 300, ife_0_csid 300; the four that
                               the vendor node asks for and at their rates
    the settle count           swept from 20 to 48, which covers the window of
                               the standard (27 to 47), without moving a bit
    the MediaTek table         compared with the vendor one: zero registers in
                               common, it steps on nothing

This adds four module parameters -op_pll_mult, op_pre_div, op_sys_div and
carriles- that are written AFTER the mode table, which is what programs the
PLLs, and before starting the stream. With the front camera the same mechanism
made it possible to sweep eight rates in one afternoon instead of one per build.

The lane count is added as well because it is the other thing the CSIPHY and the
sensor have to agree on, and trying 2 against 3 without recompiling separates
"the sensor does not emit properly" from "the PHY listens wrong".
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/imx682.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/imx682.c
@@ -403,6 +403,40 @@
 	},
 };
 
+/*
+ * BARRER EL ENLACE EN CALIENTE
+ * ---------------------------
+ * El link_freq de 435,2 MHz esta DEDUCIDO de los PLL del fichero de fabrica
+ * (19,2/3 x 272 / 2 / 2), no medido. Si el sensor emite a otro ritmo del que
+ * se le dice al CSIPHY, no hay sincronismo posible y el CSID no ve nada, que
+ * es exactamente lo que pasa.
+ *
+ * Con la frontal esto mismo permitio barrer ocho velocidades en una tarde en
+ * vez de una por compilacion. Se escribe justo despues de la tabla del modo y
+ * antes de arrancar la transmision, que es el unico punto donde vale.
+ *
+ * 0 = dejar el valor de la tabla de fabrica.
+ */
+static int op_pll_mult;
+module_param(op_pll_mult, int, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(op_pll_mult,
+	"Multiplicador del PLL de salida (0x030e/0x030f). 0 = tabla (272).");
+
+static int op_pre_div;
+module_param(op_pre_div, int, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(op_pre_div,
+	"Predivisor del PLL de salida (0x030d). 0 = tabla (3).");
+
+static int op_sys_div;
+module_param(op_sys_div, int, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(op_sys_div,
+	"Divisor de sistema de salida (0x030b). 0 = tabla (2).");
+
+static int carriles;
+module_param(carriles, int, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(carriles,
+	"Carriles que se le declaran al sensor en 0x0114. 0 = tabla (3).");
+
 static const s64 imx682_link_freqs[] = {
 	IMX682_LINK_FREQ,
 };
@@ -641,6 +675,26 @@
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * Los ajustes de barrido van DESPUES de la tabla del modo, que es
+	 * quien programa los PLL, y antes de arrancar la transmision.
+	 */
+	if (op_pre_div)
+		imx682_write(s, 0x030D, op_pre_div);
+	if (op_pll_mult) {
+		imx682_write(s, 0x030E, (op_pll_mult >> 8) & 0xff);
+		imx682_write(s, 0x030F, op_pll_mult & 0xff);
+	}
+	if (op_sys_div)
+		imx682_write(s, 0x030B, op_sys_div);
+	if (carriles)
+		imx682_write(s, 0x0114, carriles - 1);
+
+	if (op_pre_div || op_pll_mult || op_sys_div || carriles)
+		dev_info(&s->client->dev,
+			 "barrido: pre=%d mult=%d div=%d carriles=%d\n",
+			 op_pre_div, op_pll_mult, op_sys_div, carriles);
+
 	ret = __v4l2_ctrl_handler_setup(&s->ctrls);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
